From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Colin Lundholm <265166644+gitColinX@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:40:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zuma-husky: Give the main PMIC
 its interrupt

Without an interrupt the S2MPG14 driver supplies its rails but none of
the PMIC's events reach the host ("no interrupt, so no RTC alarm" at
boot), so rtc0 has no wake alarm on the Pixel 8 Pro. The interrupt is
GIC SPI 74, as stock's s2mpg14mfd node has it on this board
(interrupts = <0 0x4a 4>), latched by the VGPIO2AP sysreg, as the gs201
boards and the Pixel 9a have it; wakeup-source makes the alarm a wake
source for suspend, which has not been run on this phone yet.

On a Pixel 8 Pro (G1MNW) with these three commits on the display and
GPU test tree: no "no RTC alarm" line, rtc0 has wakealarm, the
s2mpg14-pmic interrupt line counts 0 until an alarm armed with
rtcwake -m no -s 60 fires on time (rtc-alarm0 0 to 1), no failed units.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Colin Lundholm <265166644+gitColinX@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts
index be6b992bb..130fe8683 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts
@@ -202,6 +202,9 @@ wifi_dma_pool: wifi-dma-pool {
 &acpm_ipc {
 	pmic-1 {
 		compatible = "samsung,s2mpg14-pmic";
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 74 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		google,vgpio2ap-sysreg = <&sysreg_vgpio2ap>;
+		wakeup-source;
 
 		regulators {
 			touch_avdd: ldo4m {
